---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { publication, secretariatEmail } from '../data/home';
import { newsletterEdition } from '../data/newsletter';
import '../styles/home.css';
const edition = newsletterEdition(publication);
---
<BaseLayout title="Research & Gateway Medical Journal — NMA Ogun" description="Discover the Gateway Medical Journal and find its journal website, manuscript submission system and newsletter research discussions.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Research & publication" title="Knowledge shared. Practice strengthened." description="Connect with research, professional reflection and the publication opportunities introduced in NMA Ogun’s biannual newsletter." />
  <section class="container page-section issue-messages"><article><p class="eyebrow">Gateway Medical Journal</p><h2>A journal for medical<br />and health scholarship.</h2><p>The Third Edition, 2026 newsletter introduces the Gateway Medical Journal as a journal published by the Nigerian Medical Association, Ogun State. It describes a scope including original research, reviews, case reports, professional perspectives and related medical and health contributions.</p><div class="home-link-row"><a class="button" href="https://www.gatemedjournal.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit the journal website ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://www.ejmanager.com/my/gmj/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the manuscript system ↗</a></div><p class="newsletter-note">Use the journal’s own current instructions for article types, manuscript preparation, review, fees and publication arrangements.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">For prospective contributors</p><h2>Choose the right<br />editorial channel.</h2><p>Journal manuscripts and newsletter contributions have separate purposes and editorial processes. Send research manuscripts through the journal’s published submission system. For association news, reflections, photographs or future newsletter contributions, enquire through the Secretariat.</p><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${secretariatEmail}?subject=Research%20or%20newsletter%20enquiry`}>Ask the Secretariat ↗</a></article></section>
  {edition && <section class="container page-section"><p class="eyebrow">From the biannual newsletter</p><h2>Explore the research discussion.</h2><div class="issue-card-grid"><article class="issue-card"><h3>Journal information</h3><p>Read the journal introduction and submission guidance published in this edition.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${edition.href}#page=51`}>Read the newsletter’s journal page ↗</a></article><article class="issue-card"><h3>Evidence and professional debate</h3><p>The issue includes a discussion of HTLV-1 blood donor screening, with the authors’ stated evidence limitations.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${edition.href}#page=39`}>Read the original research discussion ↗</a></article><article class="issue-card"><h3>Digital medicine and education</h3><p>Read the edition’s contributions on digital pathology, responsible innovation and professional learning.</p><a class="text-link" href="/newsletter/2026-third-edition#features">Explore newsletter features ↗</a></article></div></section>}
</BaseLayout>
